# vehje-runtime-driver, known gaps

## no-std

The crate root carries `#![cfg_attr(not(feature = "std"), no_std)]`
with `default = ["std"]`. The driver opens the Zig runtime dylib
through `std::fs` paths and (future) `libloading`, both of which
require std. The no_std variant is reserved for the embedded-target
future where dylib dispatch is replaced with statically linked
extension slots. The lint pack reads only the literal `#![no_std]`
attribute and does not recognise the cfg_attr form yet; refinement
is parked under a future mockspace task. Until then this gap is
documented and accepted.
